-- FastAPI
-- Build the image Dev PC and transfer to Production Server.
-- Not required Internet in Server
🚀 Step 1: Create FastAPI project (on Dev PC)

Create a folder:

mkdir fastapi-app
cd fastapi-app
🔹 main.py
from fastapi import FastAPI

app = FastAPI()

@app.get("/")
def read_root():
    return {"message": "FastAPI is working!"}

@app.get("/hello/{name}")
def say_hello(name: str):
    return {"message": f"Hello {name}"}

🐳Create requirements.txt

vim requirements.txt

fastapi
uvicorn

🐳 Step 2: Create Dockerfile
FROM python:3.11-slim

WORKDIR /app

COPY requirements.txt .
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt

COPY . .

CMD ["uvicorn", "main:app", "--host", "0.0.0.0", "--port", "8000"]
🔨 Step 3: Build Docker Image (Dev PC)
docker build -t fastapi-app:latest .

Test locally:

docker run -p 8000:8000 fastapi-app

Open:

http://localhost:8000




🚀 1. Build Image (Dev PC)

Inside your FastAPI project folder:

docker build -t self-hosted-ai-starter-kit-fastapi:latest .

Verify:

docker images

You should see:

self-hosted-ai-starter-kit-fastapi   latest
📦 2. Save Image to File

Export it as .tar:

docker save -o self-hosted-ai-starter-kit-fastapi.tar self-hosted-ai-starter-kit-fastapi:latest

3. Transfer to Server
Using SCP:
scp self-hosted-ai-starter-kit-fastapi.tar user@server:/home/user/

OR use:

WinSCP
USB drive
shared folder


📥 4. Load Image (Server)

SSH into your server:

docker load -i self-hosted-ai-starter-kit-fastapi.tar

Check:

docker images


5. Run Container
docker run -d -p 8000:8000 \
  --name fastapi-service \
  self-hosted-ai-starter-kit-fastapi:latest

or Add the below in docker compose.yaml at the end

fastapi:
    image: self-hosted-ai-starter-kit-fastapi:latest
    container_name: fastapi
    hostname: fastapi
    networks: ['demo']
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - 8000:8000   # optional (remove in production if using proxy)


🌐 6. Test API

Open:

http://server-ip:8000

